<title>USA: J. Ray McDermott unit gets $40 mln contract.</title>
<headline>J. Ray McDermott unit gets $40 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDermott Marine Construction Ltd said Friday it has received a $40 million contract for the design, procurement, fabrication, installation and pre-commissioning of a six-well subsea development in the British North Sea's Kingfisher Field.</p>
<p>McDermott Marine is a unit of J. Ray McDermott SA. It said it received the contract from Shell U.K. Exploration and Production, a subsidiary of the Royal Dutch/Shell Group. The work is expected to be completed in the fourth quarter of 1997. The Kingfisher Field is a high pressure, sour gas and condensate development.</p>
</text>
